  },
  "cover": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "datasheet - \"Horizontal Manager with Molded Fingers and Hinging Cover, 4RU\" (the data sheet's Product Description). The cover is its own part, fitted as shipped, so a drawing can take it off and show the fingers (the `cover-off` configuration). The format has no hinge, so which edge it swings on and its hinge are a gap; no mechanism is invented."
  },
  "ears": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - the 16.3 of ear each end is half of the 32.6 between the 450.0 the manager's body is taken to fill (the EIA-310 clear opening between the rails, 17.72 in) and the 482.6 overall. No Belden document gives the ear width or its holes, so the ears are the ends of the back plate and are drawn with it, with no holes."
  },
  "fingers": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - MOLDED FINGERS ALONG THE TOP AND THE BOTTOM EDGE OF THE FRONT, EACH A ROW OF ELEVEN WITH TEN OPENINGS. The BHH192UR thumbnail, the clearest of the family, shows the finger rods standing from the back plate to the cover along the top, ten openings counted across; the BHH194UR thumbnail is too small to count again, and its 4U height is carried by the finger plate and the cover, not by more fingers. Its bottom row is read as the top's again. The count, ten, may be out by one. 42.5 pitch, a 34.0 opening and an 8.5 finger, each read as proportions of the 450.0 between the ears; the finger plate is 10.0 thick. THE THUMBNAILS SHOW NO ROW OF FINGERS AT THE REAR of the 7.22 in depth, only the back plate and its flange, so no rear row is modelled: it is not stated either way."
  },
  "front": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - the cover, fitted, over the two rows of finger ends. The `duct` guide is the 157.8 between the finger plates (177.8 less 2 x 10.0), over the 450.0 between the ears."
  },
  "guides": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - the duct on the front view is the channel between the finger plates, run across the rack; finger pitch 42.5 and opening 34.0 as `fingers`."
  },
  "left": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - the side: the back plate, the two finger plates 10.0 high with the channel between, and the cover's face and returns at the front. No picture of the maker's is a side elevation; it is built from the thumbnails and the data sheet's table. The right is the same, turned round."
  },
  "method": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "FIGURES FROM A DATA SHEET TABLE AND FROM A THUMBNAIL. The BHH194UR technical data sheet (revision 0.47, 05-31-2024) states the rack units, the overall height, width and depth, the weight, the material and the finish, and carries one thumbnail of the part, too small to count a row on. NO BELDEN DOCUMENT HOLDS A DIMENSIONED DRAWING: the manufacturer's product page, the one page the issue found for this part, returned a Cloudflare challenge (403) to the one request made, and the catalog page is a script shell with no content, so the product photographs were not reached. Every figure below that is not the data sheet's table is read off the thumbnails of the BHH192UR and BHH193UR, which are one CAD render in grey and not a photograph, and is `estimated`, with how. Nothing was copied from a thumbnail; the figures are transcribed. The data sheet's footer (\"Although Belden makes every reasonable effort ... provided on an AS IS basis\") grants no licence to reuse its artwork, so only its figures are used."
  },
  "mount": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - the data sheet says the part is a 19 in rack mount with mounting hardware included and shows no figure of how it bolts. Its depth reaches 7.22 in past the rail face, so it is taken as a `rack-face` part that bolts to the rail face at a rack unit and stands out from it, as the Chatsworth Evolution managers are. Whether the line is `rack-face` or `rack` is a choice the pull request asks the owner to accept."
  },
  "rear": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - the back of the plate, plain. The thumbnails show its upper edge as a flange with two steps and a row of notches at one end of the section, which are not drawn: they are seen too small to read. No Belden document shows the back of the part."
  },
  "shell": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - A SHEET BODY, NOT A BOX: the back plate as a well 181.9 deep, the two rows of fingers standing in it, the cover in it across the finger heads, which opens and lifts off. The data sheet says \"Steel and Plastic Molded Fingers\" and nothing of the plate's construction."
  },
  "thickness": {
